                <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;: A ticket is created only when the customer confirms it (or reports the guidance unresolved); critical concerns skip the KB and go straight to an urgent ticket. Every ticket write (API, visual confirm, agent tools) lands in the tickets table; its stream is the only source of ticket events, so alerts, customer emails and the diagnostics workflow (started once per ticket, execution name = ticket ID) apply to every path, with retries and one dead-letter queue. Events and emails carry no ticket content. Backups: point-in-time recovery plus daily full exports of both ticket tables to S3 (35-day expiry). Photos are stored and analysed in us-east-1 while KB, AgentCore and Nova Lite run in eu-north-1 (cross-region; data-residency approval needed). The agent lane reuses Agent 1 and the existing ticket logic and tables (target and writes default to off)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=11;spacing=4;fontColor=#232F3E;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="220" y="2297" width="2220" height="92" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
